e  public  we must use language that everyone can  understand  and it is crucial today that we extend  our skills and efforts  to a broad spectrum of audiences via a  variety of outlets  be a traditional media and social media  among others  to which people get their information  now putting all these principles into  practice  is essential to building public trust  and science  as the pathway to resolving  the covet 19 pandemic and ensuring  that the fruits of our research such as  vaccines  have the greatest potential benefit  in this regard we can be heartened by  the rapid pace of scientific progress  including  extremely encouraging data showing a  high degree of efficacy  for candidate covert 19 vaccines in  large-scale  clinical trials never  has a vaccine been developed in so short  of time  of course a vaccine may will not be  and certainly is not a magic solution  by itself for some time  we still will need to adhere to simple  public health measures  such as universal masking physical  distancing  and avoiding crowds that we know these  things work  to stem virus spread getting the  messages out about the value  of proven low tech covert 19 prevention  tools  in clear credible and coherent ways  will continue to be a communications  challenge  once covert 19 vaccines are approved to  deploy  which could be actually as early as the  end of this year  there will be powerful tools for us now  to help us protect the vulnerable and  gradually help quell and eventually  end the coven 19 pandemic for everyone  and thus heal and restore  our upended lives once again  we have formidable communication  challenges ahead of us  as we work to convey with honesty  transparency and clarity  the benefits of vaccination to sometimes  very skeptical audiences i imagine  some of the jmc school students watching  today  will contribute important articles radio  and tv segments  and other communications products to  these  important issues some of you have  already have i'm s